      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release 2,550 mg, extended-release 2,000 mg).\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg per dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check whether you meant one of these:\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg** twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg** to **1000 mg** twice daily, titrated up\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a note with the rationale, and the order may need pharmacy review."
      }
